#!args --verify-dirty
# scroll copies (lib/ui/scrollcopy.rs) in the data views: when only a view's content moved, the
# pixels still shown are moved in the framebuffer and the rest is drawn; every frame is compared
# with a full redraw (--verify-dirty), `expect scrollcopy N` counts the frames that copied.  A
# script renders after each input event and a view gets its content grid once it moves, so the
# second frame that moves it copies.  The side panel (a scroll view with cards, a tree, meters;
# it scrolls by 96 DIP in a low window), by the wheel and frame by frame while it scrolls
# smoothly (bench anim: every frame checked after its timed render)
size 1440 560
wait 50
move 1200,400
wait 50
wheel 1200,400 -120
wait 300
wheel 1200,400 -120
wait 300
wheel 1200,400 -120
wait 300
move 1200,410
expect #30610 value 96
expect scrollcopy 1
wheel 1200,410 240
bench 12 anim
expect_nowarn
